<article class="panel prose">
  <h1>How Yard Marketplace works</h1>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><strong>Create an account.</strong> Buyers and sellers both sign in, so you always know who you're dealing with.</li>
    <li><strong>Post your item.</strong> Add photos, a price and a description. It shows up in search right away.</li>
    <li><strong>Chat.</strong> Buyers message sellers directly from the listing. Every conversation stays in your inbox.</li>
    <li><strong>Pay inside Yard.</strong> The buyer pays from their Yard wallet. The money is held in <em>escrow</em> — the seller can see it's paid, but can't touch it yet.</li>
    <li><strong>Hand over the item.</strong> The seller ships it or meets up, and marks the order as shipped.</li>
    <li><strong>Confirm &amp; release.</strong> The buyer confirms they received it, and the money is released to the seller's wallet. Sellers can withdraw at any time.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2 id="safety">Safety &amp; escrow</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>If the seller cancels, or the buyer cancels before the item has shipped, the buyer gets a full refund automatically.</li>
    <li>If something goes wrong after shipping, message the other person first. If you can't sort it out, report the listing and an administrator can step in and refund the order.</li>
    <li>Never pay outside of Yard. Escrow only protects payments made inside the site.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2 id="rules">Marketplace rules</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No illegal, stolen, counterfeit or dangerous items, weapons, drugs, or live animals.</li>
    <li>Listings must show the actual item and be honest about its condition.</li>
    <li>Be respectful in messages. Harassment, scams and spam get you banned.</li>
    <li>Administrators can remove listings and suspend accounts that break these rules. Open orders of suspended accounts are refunded.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="notice">Demo note: wallet deposits and withdrawals are simulated in this version — no real card is charged. See the README to connect a real payment provider.</p>
</article>
